# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# kinds.mkind - English-pack kind-atom surface forms.
#
# English is the canonical ontology language, so for a kind whose ontology hstr
# already IS the desired surface word ("history", "music") no entry is needed -
# the lookup falls back to the canonical hstr. This file exists for the kinds
# whose surface form differs from the bare hstr: multi-word atoms the hstr packs
# with underscores ("knife_fighting" -> "knife fighting"), and atoms that read
# more naturally as a different noun ("poisoning_knowledge" -> "poisons"). It
# also keeps English symmetric with the other packs (every language owns its
# kind vocabulary in one file) and is the single home for future surface
# variants - phrasing / educational-band / cultural-background forms ride the
# same per-entry tag mechanism the agreement variants (.m/.f/.cg/.nt/.pl) use.
#
# Syntax: `<canonical>[.<tag>...] <localized>`. The localized form may contain
# spaces. Same-axis last-wins; an untagged entry is the unmarked default.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# === domain axis (interest / skilled_in / calling targets) ===================
# Concepts.mon `domain` subtree. The interest band is the prominent description
# element, so the whole axis is owned here for a clean, browsable vocabulary.

# academic_field
classics                      classics
engineering                   engineering
medicine                      medicine
law                           law
theology                      theology
commerce                      commerce
natural_science               natural science
accountancy                   accountancy
navigation                    navigation
husbandry                     husbandry
primary_school_curriculum     primary schooling
secondary_school_curriculum   secondary schooling
history                       history
science                       science

# performance_art
music                         music
theatre                       theatre
literature                    literature

# martial
marksmanship                  marksmanship
knife_fighting                knife fighting
swordsmanship                 swordsmanship
pugilism                      pugilism
wrestling                     wrestling
horsemanship                  horsemanship
riding                        riding

# illicit
poisoning_knowledge           poisons
forgery                       forgery
lockpicking                   lockpicking
climbing                      climbing
evading                       evasion
detecting                     detective work

# athletics
sports                        sports

# avocation / devotional / civic
antiques                      antiques
religion                      religion
spiritualism                  spiritualism
suffrage                      suffrage

# === nationality (proper adjectives - the realize layer title-cases) =========
# The single-word ones already capitalise correctly from the canonical hstr;
# st_revieran needs an explicit two-word form (capitalise_first only touches the
# first letter, so the second word is pre-capitalised here).
st_revieran                   St Revieran
